  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "When using continuous synching on a enum value using [UdonSynced(UdonSyncMode.None)] when ownership is changed and the value is altered, the sent out value to non-owners of the udonbehaviour is interpolated, for example 2 being changed to 0 results in a 1 being sent to other clients and then on next synch it changes to the intended 0. \n\nAlso to note i was using changefieldcallback functions with this.\n\nI specialize in making general purpose coding intended for both end users and coders, as such i add in error logs for when invalid actions occur, this time i was working on a condition dependant statemachine using enumerations and this bug was caught in one of these traps and logged. It is possible this bug also affects regular values and not only enumerations, i am speculating this bug is the result of a minor oversight when implementing enumerations, and if this the case should be easy to fix.",
